        <section class="border-t border-[#2a2038] pt-10" aria-labelledby="initial"><h2 id="initial" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100">2. Initial working model</h2><p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">Read the supplied functions and fixtures before filling the model gaps. Make the smallest domain decisions that let the program typecheck, then run it. Do not turn the types into broad strings merely to make the compiler quiet.</p><ol class="mt-5 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400"><li>Inspect <code>src/model.ts</code>, <code>src/operations.ts</code>, and <code>src/main.ts</code>.</li><li>Complete <code>UserSummary</code>, <code>Project</code>, <code>Issue</code>, create/update inputs, finite status/priority values, and <code>RequestState&lt;T&gt;</code>.</li><li>Run <code>npm run typecheck</code>, then <code>npm run run</code>.</li><li>Record what <code>T</code> connects and why update is not simply <code>Partial&lt;Issue&gt;</code>.</li></ol></section>
        <section class="border-t border-[#2a2038] pt-10" aria-labelledby="change"><h2 id="change" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100">3. Change request: assignee becomes a preview</h2><p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">The old model stores <code>assigneeId?: number</code>. Change it to <code>assignee: UserSummary | null</code>: the trusted entity always has an assignee field, and <code>null</code> means deliberately unassigned. An update can still omit <code>assignee</code> to mean “leave it unchanged.”</p><p class="mt-4 font-semibold text-[#d9c9ff]">Change the model, then run <code>npm run typecheck</code> before touching callers. Treat diagnostics as a map of stale assumptions.</p><label class="mt-6 block text-sm font-semibold text-gray-200">Which failures appeared, and what assumption did each expose?<textarea required data-b02-draft="diagnostics" class="mt-3 min-h-36 w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-[#0a0d12] p-4 font-mono text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-gray-100 focus:border-[#c4a7ff] focus:outline-none" placeholder="operations.ts: … assumed …"></textarea></label><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-500">Do not add imaginary union members or widen the model just to erase a diagnostic. Decide whether the contract or the dependent code is wrong, then repair it.</p></section>
        <section class="border-t border-[#2a2038] pt-10" aria-labelledby="boundary"><h2 id="boundary" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100">4. Recover the runtime boundary</h2><p class="mt-2 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-gray-400">A separate payload is <code>unknown</code>. Finish <code>parseIssuePreview</code> by checking object shape and every field, then constructing a fresh trusted preview. A TypeScript type does not validate JSON.</p><pre class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg bg-[#111019] p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-[#d9c9ff]"><code>npm run test:parser
npm run typecheck
npm run run</code></pre><p class="mt-4 text-sm text-gray-500">The parser must not use <code>any</code>, a blind assertion, or a fixture identity shortcut.</p></section>
        <section class="border-t border-[#2a2038] pt-10" aria-labelledby="recall"><h2 id="recall" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100">5. Explain after the build</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-7 text-gray-400">Answer without notes first. Your drafts stay in this browser.</p><div class="mt-6 space-y-5"><?php foreach (['Describe the entity, create, and update contracts—and where null versus absence is deliberate.', 'Which values are finite, what relationship does RequestState<T> preserve, and what did the assignee change expose?', 'Where is the runtime trust boundary? What did typecheck prove, and what did parser tests prove?'] as $i => $question): ?><label class="block text-sm font-semibold text-gray-200"><?= ($i + 1) . '. ' . htmlspecialchars($question) ?><textarea required data-b02-draft="explain-<?= $i ?>" class="mt-3 min-h-28 w-full rounded-lg border border-gray-700 bg-[#0a0d12] p-3 text-sm font-normal leading-6 text-gray-100 focus:border-[#c4a7ff] focus:outline-none"></textarea></label><?php endforeach; ?></div></section>
        <section class="border-t border-[#2a2038] pt-10" aria-labelledby="help"><h2 id="help" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-100">Hints, reference, and closed-book checkpoint</h2><div class="mt-5 space-y-3"><?php foreach ([['Hint 1 — where to reason','Read the uses before deciding the shape. Each consumer tells you what relationship it expects.'],['Hint 2 — retrieve the concept','Ask whether each field is always present, may deliberately be empty, or can be omitted because no change was requested.'],['Hint 3 — run an experiment','After only the assignee type change, run typecheck and label each error as model change or stale caller assumption.'],['Hint 4 — small implementation clue','For an unknown object, narrow to a record, validate primitive and finite values, then return a new object from those checked values.']] as [$title, $body]): ?><details class="rounded-lg border border-[#2a2038] bg-[#111019] p-4"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-200"><?= htmlspecialchars($title) ?></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400"><?= htmlspecialchars($body) ?></p></details><?php endforeach; ?><details class="rounded-lg border border-[#2a2038] bg-[#111019] p-4"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-gray-200">Reference explanation — reveal after a meaningful attempt</summary><div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-400"><p>An entity records trusted current state; creation excludes generated identity and includes only fields required to create it. Update describes permitted changes, so <code>Partial&lt;Issue&gt;</code> is too broad because it permits an ID change.</p><p><code>description: string | null</code> means the field exists but has no description. <code>description?: string</code> means no instruction about the field was supplied. Finite unions keep invalid workflow words out of trusted code.</p><p>The assignee refactor usefully broke code that expected an ID. Those errors locate stale assumptions. <code>RequestState&lt;T&gt;</code> connects a success state to the exact data it carries. Runtime checks establish trust for untyped data; typecheck proves checked code respects its declared contracts.</p></div></details></div><div class="mt-8 space-y-3 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-300"><p class="font-semibold text-gray-100">Closed-book checkpoint</p><?php foreach (['Why is Issue different from CreateIssueInput?','Why might Partial<Issue> be a bad IssueUpdate type?','Contrast description?: string with description: string | null.','What does readonly prove at runtime?','Why is status: string weaker than a finite union?','What relationship does RequestState<T> preserve?','Why were assignee compiler failures useful?','Why is widening a union merely to silence an error dangerous?','Why must an external Issue payload be validated?','Transfer: when might a delivery address be null but omitted from an update?'] as $i => $question): ?><details class="rounded-lg border border-[#2a2038] bg-[#111019] p-4"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-gray-200"><?= ($i + 1) . '. ' . htmlspecialchars($question) ?></summary><p class="mt-3 text-gray-400">Attempt this without notes. Compare the reasoning above only after you have answered.</p></details><?php endforeach; ?></div></section>
